So I ask you, get loud, get proud. Are you ready!?"

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:21.680
The original Halo was a huge deal for Microsoft.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:32.200
Halo: Combat Evolved Rated M for Mature

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.240
It was the flagship game for their brand

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:39.600
new console the Xbox. In 2001 no one knew if Microsoft would sink or swim in the

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.760
games industry and Halo the cutting edge fast-paced first-person shooter

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:47.360
from little-known Mac developer Bungie was Microsoft the way of showing that

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.760
they knew what they were doing.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.400
"with the power of the GeForce 2 GTS shading

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.540
rasterizer plasma burns look more realistic than ever before."

00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:02.640
"Nvidia's GeForce 2 GTS and Bungie's Halo. This is the future of gaming."

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.700
The game was a hit, selling five million copies

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.200
and inspiring a small but dedicated base of competitive players.

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:42.680
Prize pools were small but players wanted organization so handful players

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:47.200
and fans banded together to create MLG an organization that would go on to make

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.720
Halo eports huge.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.600
"MLG was kind of was born out of Mike and my love of video

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.000
games." "We were sitting there and I said why don't we just run one of these

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.880
tournaments and just see how it works." "It was a leap of faith."

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:03.120
A few years later Microsoft and Bungie launched Halo 2 which was better in just about every way.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.760
The gameplay was better the maps were better even the sales were better with 8

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:11.200
million sold to Halo's five and that momentum propelled Halo to the top of

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.080
the North American esports scene. Europe had Counter-Strike and Dota. Korea had

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.360
Starcraft and NA had Halo.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:38.920
(Casting)

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:42.720
The era of Halo 2 &amp; 3 was dominated by legendary teams like

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:47.560
Carbon Final Boss and Str8 Rippin. In 2006 MLG worked out a deal with the

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:52.180
USA Network to broadcast MLG tournaments on TV and episodes were

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.980
later available on Xbox Live.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:04:08.120
(Casting)

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.680
MLG ran dozens of Halo tournaments

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:15.200
between 2005 and 2007 and only stopped to bring in Halo 3.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.640
Halo 3 cracked 14 million copies sold blowing its predecessor's out of the water and

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.780
throwing MLG's events into an even higher gear. Every Halo tournament MLG

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:29.900
ran gave it over $50,000 in prize money, higher than anything in NA at the time

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.460
with annual $280,000 championships

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:55.500
(Casting)

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:59.000
MLG quickly became the biggest esports tournament organizer

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.880
in North America off the back of their success with Halo adding Super Smash

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:08.120
Bros, Tekken, Rainbow Six, Call of Duty and
Gears of War all to varying degrees

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:08.780
of success.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.320
"What we did was go out and find all of the best kind of grassroots

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:15.520
level people who are running these great tournaments and brought them in and then

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:17.820
we really developed Major League Gaming."

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:20.080
Halo 3 was a great competitive game but only

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.020
after MLG and fans made a few small tweaks to the game's competitive

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:28.320
settings. Most notably pro players disabled equipment a new feature added

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:32.260
to Halo 3 that really changed the way the game was played but with all that

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:35.960
turned off Halo 3 was a great competitive game and it looked to be

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:40.840
carrying halo into a bright future, that is until Reach.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:44.140
"Halo Reach falls, 2010."

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:48.300
It was no secret that Bungie and Microsoft were going through a breakup Bungie

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.840
wanted independence to make new games but their agreement with Microsoft meant

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.760
that they had to make a few more Halo games before they could finally get it

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:58.960
"It's such an important cultural ideal here that this studio owns what it

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:03.340
creates." "Independence was going to be the only thing that was gonna be able to

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:07.600
allow us to do what we wanted to do." "The deal was essentially we make a couple

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.920
more Halo games we leave Halo with Microsoft and we can split amicably so I

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:17.560
mean ultimately the price of our freedom was to to leave our baby behind to move

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:20.120
from being Halo developers to Halo fans."

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.280
So Bungie took a chance to experiment.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:26.080
First came ODST, a mostly single-player game that didn't affect

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:30.700
Halo's competitive scene at all. Then in 2010 they put out Halo Reach a game that

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:34.520
carried forward Bungie's a legacy of excellent single-player campaigns but

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:38.540
evolved the equipment system from Halo 3 into something much worse for the

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:43.000
competitive scene. "You might be surprised to hear that when Halo Reach came out it

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.500
was met with backlash from the Halo community. I vividly remember the uproar

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:51.700
on the Bungie forums. There were threads upon threads of players upset with the

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:55.560
game claiming that it didn't feel like Halo and that everything that made Halo

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.720
great was gone. I vividly remember not enjoying the multiplayer for three main

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:03.020
reasons. Number one, the maps. Number two, the weapons and

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:09.460
number three, armor abilities." Reach had several problems equipment was replaced

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:12.740
by armor abilities. Abilities included active camouflage which made you

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:16.640
completely invisible. Armor lock which made you invincible before releasing a

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.240
pulse and damage and jet pack which let you fly.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:21.000
"And then there's bloom there was

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.540
sprint there was there was armor lock that was in the first MLG

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:27.620
tournament, there was jet pack and all that stuff does not belong in Halo

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:32.420
Thanks to a new bloom mechanic, full auto had no spray pattern it was entirely random

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:36.640
accuracy meant stopping which was a far cry for the way top players had

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:37.840
experienced Halo in the past.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.860
"There's so many things that are wrong with this

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:44.340
game that can be fixed in a very small amount of time and that needs to happen

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:47.820
during this four month offseason that we're gonna have with MLG, okay."

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:51.460
Bungie and later 343 Halo's new development team eventually

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:55.060
let players turn off bloom and armor abilities and even let them have default

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:58.640
starting load outs, but by then the game that competitive reach players were

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:02.240
experiencing was so far from what the average player was playing that they

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:05.860
weren't even the same game. They still ran reach but it was second to

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:09.200
Starcraft 2 and League of Legends which were quickly picking up steam in North

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:13.880
America thanks to strong development support. MLG only ran a handful of reach

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:18.320
events but the community shrank alongside their game and MLG had to

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:20.620
remove Hslo as the flagship game on their circuit.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:22.200
"The halo was just is just

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.720
headed down man."

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:27.740
But if  Reach shrank Halo's community then it was Halo 4 that

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:29.160
truly killed it.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:32.080
"We've really focused on trying to craft these moments that live

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:36.320
up to the legacy of the Halo experience." "We're working within the constraints of

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:41.220
what makes Halo Halo but trying to make every aspect of it bigger and better.

