dollars in 2016 and the 1 million dollar prize pool stuck around

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:17.020
for the next two years.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:44.480
(Casting)

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:45.920
Halo still doesn't pick up massive

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:49.420
viewership but it's in a much better place than it was even two years ago.

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:53.080
Pro teams are coming in to give pro players salaries, prize pools are

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:56.660
sustainable and viewership does trend upwards during major events.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:29.040
(Casting)

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:33.320
Put it all together and we can learn at least one important thing from Halo and it's

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:38.000
fall from grace. If you make a good game people are going to play it and if you

